WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.444
"The Exercise “Myth” for Weight Loss"

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.780
When trying to lose weight,
which is more important:

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.980
diet or exercise?

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.760
A national survey found that
a "vast majority" of Americans

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.780
trying to control their weight

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.640
believed that food
and beverage consumption

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.520
and physical activity
were equally important.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.120
Seven out of ten
went with equally important,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.640
about two out of ten thought
exercise was more important,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.740
and only about one
out of ten chose diet.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.400
The vast majority of Americans
are wrong.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.700
It's easy to understand
how people might think

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.980
diet and exercise
play equal roles.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.540
After all,
our weight is determined

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.060
by the balance of calories in
and calories out.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.920
What people may not understand

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.840
about this
energy balance equation

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.500
is we have much more power
over the "calories in" side.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.500
In fact, on a day-to-day basis
we have full control,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.240
we could choose
to eat zero calories

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.620
or 10,000 calories.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.540
But most of the "calories out"

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.180
tend to be outside
of our control.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.000
Unlike wild animals
who tend to burn

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.380
most of their calories
on activity,

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.480
about 60 percent
of our daily calories

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.460
are used up
just to keep us alive,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.600
what's called our resting,
or basal, metabolic rate,

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.540
thanks in part
to our energy-intensive brains.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.640
Even if you stayed in bed
all day,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.340
you'd still burn
more than 1,000 calories

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.280
just to fuel the basics
like thinking, breathing,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.480
keeping your heart pumping.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.720
In contrast,
even most "active" people

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.600
accrue less than two hours
of exercise a week,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.300
which may average out
to be less than 100 calories

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.680
burned off each day.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.780
That's only about 5 percent

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.000
of the total
daily energy expenditure,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.100
the "calories out" side
of the equation.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.640
So, the 2,000 calories we may
take in every day from our diet

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.640
can exert 20 times
more influence than exercise

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.040
over our weight destiny.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.180
Most people believe that
exercise is "very effective"

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.800
as a way to lose weight,

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.200
but this has been
referred to as a myth

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.400
in the scientific literature.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.720
In fact, it's been labeled

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.060
one of the most common
misconceptions

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.860
in the field of obesity.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.100
Yet virtually all
formal weight-loss guidelines

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.740
include some sort of physical
activity recommendation.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.380
Can you outrun a bad diet?

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.500
Let's see what the science says.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.140
Population studies
have certainly found

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.320
strong correlations between
physical inactivity and obesity.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.020
But does a sedentary lifestyle
lead to obesity,

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.960
or does obesity lead
to a sedentary lifestyle?

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.300
It probably works a little bit
in both directions.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.860
To prove cause and effect,

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.900
and also quantify
the relationship,

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.600
you really have to put it
to the test.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.540
Dozens of randomized
controlled trials

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.040
involving thousands
of participants

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.480
have been published
on the effects of exercise

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.800
on weight loss.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.460
Physical activity was not found
to be an effective strategy.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.140
For example,
if you look at the studies

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.420
that tried using exercise alone
to induce weight loss,

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.100
over an average
of about five months,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.440
people only lost
about three pounds.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.060
When you put
all the studies together,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.580
it looks like it took
around six weeks of exercising

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.560
to get people
to lose a single pound.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.500
That was exercise alone, though.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.480
What about as an adjunct
to diet?

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.520
If you randomize people

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.260
into a diet
and exercise intervention

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.700
versus just the diet alone,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.760
the added exercise group
does do better,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.560
but the difference
in weight loss

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.600
only averaged about two pounds.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.060
The studies lasted
between 3 and 12 months,

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.160
and all of that
extra prescribed exercise

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.740
only seemed to translate
into a few pounds.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:29.580
The two-pound difference
was statistically significant,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.560
which means we're pretty sure
it was a real effect,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.320
but losing two pounds
over a year's time

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.020
can hardly be considered
clinically significant.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.300
As a general rule,
researchers like to see

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.220
at least a five-
or six-pound drop.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.180
In a meta-analysis of 18
randomized controlled trials

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.100
lasting a minimum
of six months,

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.900
the diet-plus-exercise group

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.260
failed to significantly beat out
the diet-only group at all.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.900
There appeared to be
no long-term benefit

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.820
to encouraging people
to add exercise

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.560
to their weight-loss regimen.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.660
What is going on?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.940
Maybe exercise is just better

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.860
at preventing people
from regaining weight.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:05.460
No.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.860
The vast majority
of randomized controlled trials

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.300
examining
weight-loss maintenance

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.000
also failed to show
an exercise benefit.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.420
Part of the problem
is compliance.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.380
It's one thing
to tell people

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.180
to adhere
to an exercise regimen;

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.400
it's another thing for them
to actually do it.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.680
When the same randomized
controlled trials

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.480
were re-analyzed
to exclude people

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.920
who flouted the instructions,

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.020
and analysis was limited
to just those

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.700
who actually put in
the time and sweat,

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.400
a clear advantage
to exercise emerges.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.820
Exercise only works
if you actually do it,

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.600
though one reason people
may become rapidly disillusioned

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.860
with their new gym membership

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.840
is their gross overestimation

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.540
of the capacity of exercise
to burn off extra calories.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.660
A slice of pizza
has about 300 calories.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.380
That converts into an hour
of brisk walking per slice,

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:53.700
an hour a slice!

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.220
How many kids
are jogging two hours a day

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.600
to burn off their happy meals?

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.080
Who's got time to climb
50 flights of stairs

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.720
to take care of the calories
in just one Oreo cookie?

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.100
That's one of the reasons

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.100
that what we put in our mouths
is most important.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.620
Public health researchers
have been experimenting

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.360
with including labeling
on junk food.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.520
Which label
is more informative?

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.440
This one or these?

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.340
Still want that Toblerone
if it means you have to walk

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:20.820
two hours?

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.880
Or cookies
you'd have to skip rope

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.560
for 81 minutes for?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:30.300
I think I'd run an hour
just to avoid having to eat

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.000
shrimp-flavored potato chips.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.880
Labeling fast food menus
with little pictograms

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.820
of exercising stick figures
was found to help nudge people

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.560
towards lower calorie options.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.980
Seeing that the decision
to supersize your fries

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:47.160
would mean walking
an extra three miles that day

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.080
or that choosing
the chicken salad

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.650
over the garden salad
could mean having to run

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:52.860
nearly three miles,

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:57.260
people are more likely
to make the healthier choice.

